1
00:01:27,290 --> 00:01:29,130
See you tomorrow.

2
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:49,480
Oh, my God!

3
00:02:12,130 --> 00:02:13,630
I'm in.

4
00:04:06,750 --> 00:04:08,540
We're almost there.

5
00:04:08,710 --> 00:04:12,670
- Sir, are you sure about this? 
- I told you, we're going to be all right.

6
00:04:12,830 --> 00:04:18,300
I understand, sir. It's just that I'm scoping 
some serious sentinel activity up here.

7
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:06,930
Still can't sleep?

8
00:05:08,890 --> 00:05:10,270
You wanna talk?

9
00:05:12,600 --> 00:05:14,980
They're just dreams.

10
00:05:17,320 --> 00:05:19,690
If you're afraid of something...

11
00:05:19,860 --> 00:05:21,700
I just wish...

12
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:24,610
I wish I knew what I'm supposed to do.

13
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:26,620
That's all.

14
00:05:27,530 --> 00:05:29,120
I just wish I knew.

15
00:05:29,290 --> 00:05:33,540
She's gonna call. Don't worry.

16
00:05:33,710 --> 00:05:34,750
Here you are.

17
00:05:34,920 --> 00:05:38,380
- Are we ready to go? 
- We're already late.

18
00:05:38,550 --> 00:05:43,180
These geotherms confirm 
the last transmission of the <i>Osiris.</i>

19
00:05:43,930 --> 00:05:45,590
The machines are digging.

20
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:49,560
They're boring from the surface 
down to Zion.

21
00:05:49,720 --> 00:05:52,310
- Mother-- 
- They'll avoid the perimeter defense.

22
00:05:52,480 --> 00:05:53,980
How fast are they moving?

23
00:05:54,140 --> 00:05:57,520
Control estimates their descent 
at 100 meters an hour.

24
00:05:57,690 --> 00:06:00,150
- How deep are they? 
- Almost 2000 meters.

25
00:06:00,320 --> 00:06:03,860
- What about the scans from the <i>Osiris?</i> 
- They can't be accurate.

26
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,950
- They may be. 
- It's not possible.

27
00:06:06,110 --> 00:06:08,580
That'd mean there are 
a quarter-million sentinels.

28
00:06:08,740 --> 00:06:10,240
- That's right. 
- That can't be.

29
00:06:10,410 --> 00:06:12,080
Why not?

30
00:06:12,250 --> 00:06:16,000
A sentinel for every man, 
woman and child in Zion.

31
00:06:16,960 --> 00:06:20,920
That sounds exactly like 
the thinking of a machine to me.

32
00:06:21,090 --> 00:06:23,260
Morpheus, glad you could join us.

33
00:06:23,760 --> 00:06:24,930
Niobe.

34
00:06:26,300 --> 00:06:29,680
My apologies to all. 
But as you are undoubtedly aware...

35
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:33,140
...it's become difficult to locate 
a secure broadcast position.

36
00:06:33,310 --> 00:06:36,560
- Squiddies got our best spots. 
- Lines are crawling with them.

37
00:06:36,730 --> 00:06:40,520
And if Niobe's right, in 72 hours 
there's gonna be a quarter-million more.

38
00:06:40,690 --> 00:06:41,820
What are we gonna do?

39
00:06:41,980 --> 00:06:44,280
We're gonna do what 
Commander Lock ordered.

40
00:06:44,610 --> 00:06:47,200
We'll evacuate broadcast level 
and return to Zion.

41
00:06:47,360 --> 00:06:52,490
And does the commander have a plan 
for stopping 250,000 sentinels?

42
00:06:52,660 --> 00:06:55,330
A strategy is still being formulated.

43
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:57,170
I'm sure it is.

44
00:07:12,180 --> 00:07:14,180
What do you think 
we should do, Morpheus?

45
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:16,520
- Proceed as ordered... 
- What is it?

46
00:07:16,690 --> 00:07:17,730
I don't know.

47
00:07:17,890 --> 00:07:20,690
...however, I must 
ask one of you for help.

48
00:07:20,860 --> 00:07:26,570
Some of you believe as I believe, some 
of you do not. Those of you that do...

49
00:07:26,740 --> 00:07:29,280
...know we are nearing 
the end of our struggle.

50
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:33,700
The prophecy will be fulfilled soon. 
But before it can be...

51
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:37,210
...the Oracle must be consulted.

52
00:07:45,130 --> 00:07:47,380
If we return and recharge now...

53
00:07:47,550 --> 00:07:51,300
...we can be back in 36 hours, well 
before the machines reach this depth.

54
00:07:51,510 --> 00:07:53,350
Do you understand what you're asking?

55
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:56,350
I am asking that one ship 
remain here in our place...

56
00:07:56,520 --> 00:07:59,230
...in case the Oracle 
should attempt to contact us.

57
00:07:59,390 --> 00:08:02,520
Bullshit. You're asking one of us 
to disobey a direct order.

58
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:07,240
That's right, I am. But we well know 
that the reason most of us are here...

59
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:10,030
...is because of our affinity 
for disobedience.

60
00:08:10,200 --> 00:08:12,120
What happens when you 
get back to Zion...

61
00:08:12,280 --> 00:08:14,700
...and the commander 
throws you in the stockade?

62
00:08:14,870 --> 00:08:16,080
He won't.

63
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:20,420
Goddamn it, Morpheus, 
you ain't never gonna change.

64
00:08:21,120 --> 00:08:23,880
Shit, I'll do it just to see 
what Deadbolt does to you.

65
00:08:24,040 --> 00:08:25,590
You got 36 hours.

66
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:30,220
I'm looking for Neo.

67
00:08:30,380 --> 00:08:33,760
- Never heard of him. 
- I have something for him.

68
00:08:34,970 --> 00:08:37,180
A gift.

69
00:08:37,390 --> 00:08:40,270
You see, he set me free.

70
00:08:42,560 --> 00:08:44,940
Fine, whatever. Now piss off.

71
00:08:45,480 --> 00:08:46,530
Who was that?

72
00:08:46,690 --> 00:08:48,530
How did you know someone was here?

73
00:08:48,690 --> 00:08:50,150
He gave you this.

74
00:08:55,910 --> 00:08:57,330
He said you set him free.

75
00:08:59,290 --> 00:09:01,620
Is everything all right, sir?

76
00:09:02,250 --> 00:09:04,630
The meeting is over. 
Retreat to your exits.

77
00:09:04,790 --> 00:09:07,000
- Agents are coming. 
- Agents?

78
00:09:07,460 --> 00:09:08,840
Go.

79
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:19,720
Hiya, fellas.

80
00:09:19,890 --> 00:09:21,020
- It's him. 
- The anomaly.

81
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:22,440
- Do we proceed? 
- Yes.

82
00:09:22,600 --> 00:09:25,110
- He is still-- 
- Only human.

83
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,530
Hm. Upgrades.

84
00:10:28,460 --> 00:10:31,000
- That went as expected. 
- Yes.

85
00:10:31,170 --> 00:10:33,840
It's happening exactly as before.

86
00:10:34,010 --> 00:10:36,680
Well, not exactly.

87
00:11:27,390 --> 00:11:28,850
Where are you?

88
00:11:33,530 --> 00:11:37,110
This is the <i>Nebuchadnezzar,</i> 
requesting access through Gate Three.

89
00:11:41,160 --> 00:11:45,620
<i>Nebuchadnezzar,</i> this is Zion Control. 
Maintain present velocity and stand by.

90
00:11:45,790 --> 00:11:47,290
<i>Roger that, Control.</i>

91
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:50,960
This is Control requesting immediate 
stand-down of arms at Gate Three.

92
00:11:51,750 --> 00:11:54,960
We have the <i>Nebuchadnezzar</i> 
on approach. Let's open her up.

93
00:12:00,550 --> 00:12:03,470
<i>You are cleared through 
Gate Three to Bay Seven.</i>

94
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:05,350
Roger that, Control.

95
00:12:12,480 --> 00:12:15,570
Door's open, bed's made. 
Welcome home.

96
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:18,490
No place like it.

97
00:12:32,670 --> 00:12:36,380
Roger that, Control. Zion Control, 
stand by for Gate Three lockdown.

98
00:13:25,890 --> 00:13:28,310
<i>The</i> Nebuchadnezzar <i>is down. 
Bay Seven.</i>

99
00:13:28,470 --> 00:13:29,640
Understood.

100
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:40,900
Captain Mifune.

101
00:13:41,990 --> 00:13:43,150
Captain Morpheus.

102
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:46,160
Are you here to escort me 
to the stockade, captain?

103
00:13:46,320 --> 00:13:47,990
- I'm just here to keep the peace. 
-

104
00:13:48,790 --> 00:13:50,620
- Link. 
- Sir?

105
00:13:50,790 --> 00:13:53,370
I want the ship ready to go 
as soon as possible.

106
00:13:53,540 --> 00:13:55,080
Understood, sir.

107
00:14:17,230 --> 00:14:20,530
- Morpheus. 
- Commander Lock.

108
00:14:20,780 --> 00:14:25,280
I spoke to the other captains. I wanted to 
offer you a chance to explain your actions.

109
00:14:25,450 --> 00:14:28,320
I wasn't aware that my actions 
required any explanation.

110
00:14:28,490 --> 00:14:30,790
You were given an order 
to return to Zion.

111
00:14:30,950 --> 00:14:33,790
- I did. 
- You asked for one ship to remain behind.

112
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:36,620
I would have stayed, 
but I needed to recharge my ship.

113
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:39,500
So you admit to a direct contravention 
of your duty.

114
00:14:39,670 --> 00:14:43,090
We need a presence inside the Matrix 
to await contact from the Oracle.

115
00:14:43,260 --> 00:14:45,220
I don't want to hear that shit!

116
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:48,050
I don't care about oracles 
or prophecies or messiahs!

117
00:14:48,220 --> 00:14:51,640
I care about one thing: Stopping that 
army from destroying this city.

118
00:14:51,810 --> 00:14:54,640
To do that I need soldiers 
to obey my orders.

119
00:14:54,810 --> 00:14:59,400
With all due respect, commander, 
there is only one way to save our city.

120
00:14:59,560 --> 00:15:00,980
How?

121
00:15:01,150 --> 00:15:03,940
- Neo. 
- Goddamn it, Morpheus.

122
00:15:04,110 --> 00:15:06,740
Not everyone believes what you believe.

123
00:15:06,910 --> 00:15:08,990
My beliefs do not require them to.

124
00:15:17,170 --> 00:15:21,090
There's a gathering tonight. Everyone's 
talking. A lot of people are scared.

125
00:15:21,250 --> 00:15:24,010
No one remembers the last time 
so many ships were docked.

126
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:27,130
- Something big is happening, isn't it? 
- Hey.

127
00:15:27,300 --> 00:15:30,470
We're not allowed to say anything, 
so stop asking.

128
00:15:35,770 --> 00:15:38,900
Goddamn, it's good to be home.

129
00:15:57,620 --> 00:16:00,040
- Councillor Hamann. 
- Commander.

130
00:16:00,710 --> 00:16:03,420
- Captain. 
- Councillor.

131
00:16:03,590 --> 00:16:06,960
Council's asked me to speak tonight 
at the temple gathering.

132
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:11,220
The presence of the fleet and the 
persistence of rumors must be addressed.

133
00:16:11,390 --> 00:16:13,890
The people must be told 
what is happening.

134
00:16:14,060 --> 00:16:15,770
Of course, councillor.

135
00:16:16,470 --> 00:16:21,730
But might I advise a level of discretion 
concerning specific details.

136
00:16:21,900 --> 00:16:24,900
- We do not wish to start a panic. 
- Quite right.

137
00:16:25,070 --> 00:16:28,150
A panic is not what anyone wants.

138
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:31,660
What about you, captain? 
What would you advise?

139
00:16:34,080 --> 00:16:38,830
The truth. No one will panic, 
because there is nothing to fear.

140
00:16:38,080 --> 00:16:41,120
That army won't reach 
the gates of Zion.

141
00:16:41,920 --> 00:16:45,500
- What makes you so sure? 
- Consider what we have seen, councillor.

142
00:16:45,670 --> 00:16:47,550
Consider that in the past six months...

143
00:16:47,710 --> 00:16:49,760
...we have freed more minds 
than in six years.

144
00:16:49,920 --> 00:16:52,930
This attack is an act of desperation.

145
00:16:53,090 --> 00:16:56,930
I believe very soon the prophecy 
will be fulfilled and this war will end.

146
00:16:58,810 --> 00:17:00,940
I hope you're right, captain.

147
00:17:01,100 --> 00:17:03,810
I do not believe it to be 
a matter of hope, councillor.

148
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:06,570
It is simply a matter of time.

149
00:17:08,740 --> 00:17:10,190
My stop.

150
00:17:10,360 --> 00:17:11,780
See you soon.

151
00:17:11,950 --> 00:17:13,410
Hopefully not too soon.

152
00:17:13,570 --> 00:17:16,740
Let's go, kid. 
These two got things to do.

153
00:17:26,170 --> 00:17:27,920
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

154
00:17:28,090 --> 00:17:30,510
I am if you're thinking 
this elevator is too slow.

155
00:17:30,670 --> 00:17:34,010
- How long do we charge the <i>Neb?</i> 
- Twenty-four, maybe 30 hours.

156
00:17:34,180 --> 00:17:38,390
Some people go their entire lives 
without hearing news that good.

157
00:18:02,830 --> 00:18:07,170
Neo, please, I have a son, 
Jacob, aboard the <i>Gnosis.</i>

158
00:18:07,340 --> 00:18:10,840
- Please, watch over him. 
- I'll try.

159
00:18:11,010 --> 00:18:13,090
I have a daughter on the <i>Icarus.</i>

160
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,180
No, wait.

161
00:18:15,340 --> 00:18:17,850
It's all right. They need you.

162
00:18:18,010 --> 00:18:20,260
- I need you. 
- I know.

163
00:18:20,810 --> 00:18:23,100
There's time.

164
00:18:35,400 --> 00:18:38,830
- They started yet? 
- Only Councillor Hamann's opening prayer.

165
00:18:38,990 --> 00:18:42,080
Tonight, let us honor 
these men and women.

166
00:18:42,250 --> 00:18:44,870
These are our soldiers, our warriors.

167
00:18:45,040 --> 00:18:49,290
These are our husbands and wives, 
our brothers and sisters...

168
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:51,130
...our children.

169
00:18:51,710 --> 00:18:54,840
Let us remember those 
that have been lost...

170
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:58,220
...and let us give thanks 
for those that have been found...

171
00:18:58,390 --> 00:19:01,680
...and who stand here beside us.

172
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:05,560
Now I would like someone else 
to close this prayer...

173
00:19:05,730 --> 00:19:08,940
...someone who hasn't spoken here 
in a long time...

174
00:19:09,110 --> 00:19:14,490
...but who I believe has something to say 
that we all need to hear.

175
00:19:15,490 --> 00:19:17,070
I give you Morpheus.

176
00:19:36,590 --> 00:19:40,760
Zion! Hear me!

177
00:19:41,760 --> 00:19:44,890
It is true what many of you have heard.

178
00:19:45,060 --> 00:19:49,060
The machines have gathered 
an army, and as I speak...

179
00:19:49,230 --> 00:19:53,150
...that army is drawing nearer to our home.

180
00:19:54,610 --> 00:19:59,280
Believe me when I say we have 
a difficult time ahead of us.

181
00:19:59,950 --> 00:20:06,120
But if we are to be prepared for it, 
we must first shed our fear of it.

182
00:20:06,620 --> 00:20:11,540
I stand here before you now 
truthfully unafraid.

183
00:20:12,130 --> 00:20:13,880
Why?

184
00:20:14,300 --> 00:20:17,130
Because I believe something you do not?

185
00:20:17,300 --> 00:20:19,130
No!

186
00:20:19,430 --> 00:20:24,390
I stand here without fear 
because I remember.

187
00:20:24,560 --> 00:20:28,480
I remember that I am here not because 
of the path that lies before me...

188
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:31,980
...but because of the path 
that lies behind me.

189
00:20:32,150 --> 00:20:36,820
I remember that for 100 years 
we have fought these machines.

190
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:41,740
I remember that for 100 years 
they have sent their armies to destroy us.

191
00:20:41,910 --> 00:20:47,080
And after a century of war, 
I remember that which matters most:

192
00:20:48,870 --> 00:20:51,870
We are still here!

193
00:20:58,590 --> 00:21:00,680
Tonight...

194
00:21:00,840 --> 00:21:04,220
...let us send a message to that army.

195
00:21:04,390 --> 00:21:07,430
Tonight, let us shake this cave.

196
00:21:07,600 --> 00:21:11,480
Tonight, let us tremble these halls...

197
00:21:11,640 --> 00:21:14,770
...of earth, steel and stone.

198
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:20,190
Let us be heard from red core 
to black sky.

199
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:24,910
Tonight, let us make them remember:

200
00:21:25,070 --> 00:21:30,040
This is Zion and we are not afraid!

201
00:22:08,030 --> 00:22:09,870
Excuse me.

202
00:22:21,710 --> 00:22:25,220
- I missed you. 
- I can tell.

203
00:22:25,680 --> 00:22:29,390
I was thinking, everyone is here.

204
00:22:29,930 --> 00:22:32,220
Follow me.

205
00:25:53,220 --> 00:25:56,800
Neo, what is it?

206
00:25:57,100 --> 00:25:59,350
What's wrong?

207
00:26:00,930 --> 00:26:03,270
It's okay, you can tell me.

208
00:26:03,640 --> 00:26:06,150
Trinity...

209
00:26:06,310 --> 00:26:09,110
Don't be afraid.

210
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:11,610
I can't lose you.

211
00:26:11,780 --> 00:26:13,650
You're not gonna lose me.

212
00:26:17,780 --> 00:26:20,660
You feel this?

213
00:26:20,830 --> 00:26:22,620
I'm never letting go.

214
00:26:59,830 --> 00:27:02,490
Good night, Zion.

215
00:27:02,660 --> 00:27:05,330
Sweet dreams.

216
00:27:15,510 --> 00:27:17,180
- You all right? 
- I'll make it.

217
00:27:17,340 --> 00:27:19,970
Did you see that agent? 
I've never seen anything like that.

218
00:27:20,140 --> 00:27:22,220
It doesn't matter. 
All that matters is this.

219
00:27:22,390 --> 00:27:24,680
You first.

220
00:27:35,570 --> 00:27:38,450
- Oh, God. 
- "Smith" will suffice.

221
00:27:50,380 --> 00:27:53,670
- Thank you. 
- My pleasure.

222
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:46,930
- Care for some company? 
- Councillor Hamann.

223
00:28:47,810 --> 00:28:50,640
I don't want to intrude 
if you'd prefer to be alone.

224
00:28:51,100 --> 00:28:54,650
- No, I could probably use some company. 
- Good.

225
00:28:55,110 --> 00:28:57,480
So could I.

226
00:29:00,610 --> 00:29:03,120
It's nice tonight.

227
00:29:03,620 --> 00:29:06,030
Very calm.

228
00:29:06,200 --> 00:29:08,950
It feels like everyone is sleeping 
very peacefully.

229
00:29:09,330 --> 00:29:11,790
Not everyone.

230
00:29:12,080 --> 00:29:16,800
I hate sleeping. 
I never sleep more than a few hours.

231
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:21,010
I figure I slept the first 11 years 
of my life, now I'm making up for it.

232
00:29:21,470 --> 00:29:26,180
- What about you? 
- I just haven't been able to sleep much.

233
00:29:27,640 --> 00:29:30,810
- It's a good sign. 
- Of what?

234
00:29:30,980 --> 00:29:34,150
That you are in fact still human.

235
00:29:37,730 --> 00:29:41,650
Have you ever been 
to the engineering level?

236
00:29:41,820 --> 00:29:44,870
I love to walk there at night. 
It's quite amazing.

237
00:29:45,030 --> 00:29:47,580
- Would you like to see it? 
- Sure.

238
00:29:58,250 --> 00:30:02,720
Almost no one comes down here. 
Unless, of course, there's a problem.

239
00:30:02,880 --> 00:30:07,970
That's how it is with people. Nobody cares 
how it works as long as it works.

240
00:30:08,140 --> 00:30:10,430
I like it down here.

241
00:30:10,600 --> 00:30:16,400
I like to be reminded this city survives 
because of these machines.

242
00:30:16,560 --> 00:30:21,690
These machines are keeping us alive 
while other machines are coming to kill us.

243
00:30:22,110 --> 00:30:26,950
Interesting, isn't it? 
The power to give life...

244
00:30:27,120 --> 00:30:30,330
- ...and the power to end it. 
- We have the same power.

245
00:30:30,490 --> 00:30:33,210
Yeah, I suppose we do, but...

246
00:30:33,370 --> 00:30:36,830
...sometimes I think about those people 
still plugged into the Matrix.

247
00:30:37,000 --> 00:30:40,000
And when I look at these machines...

248
00:30:40,170 --> 00:30:45,260
...I can't help thinking that, in a way, 
we are plugged into them.

249
00:30:45,550 --> 00:30:48,430
But we control these machines, 
they don't control us.

250
00:30:48,850 --> 00:30:51,850
Of course not. How could they?

251
00:30:52,020 --> 00:30:54,560
The idea is pure nonsense...

252
00:30:55,060 --> 00:30:58,190
...but it does make one wonder just...

253
00:30:58,360 --> 00:30:59,940
...what is control?

254
00:31:00,190 --> 00:31:03,240
If we wanted, we could 
shut these machines down.

255
00:31:03,610 --> 00:31:08,070
Of course. That's it. You hit it. 
That's control, isn't it?

256
00:31:08,700 --> 00:31:12,080
If we wanted, 
we could smash them to bits.

257
00:31:12,330 --> 00:31:16,460
Although if we did, we'd have to consider 
what would happen to our lights...

258
00:31:16,620 --> 00:31:19,290
...our heat, our air.

259
00:31:20,290 --> 00:31:24,420
So we need machines and they need us. 
Is that your point, councillor?

260
00:31:24,590 --> 00:31:27,220
No. No point.

261
00:31:27,930 --> 00:31:32,010
Old men like me don't bother 
with making points. There's no point.

262
00:31:32,810 --> 00:31:36,600
Is that why there are no young men 
on the Council?

263
00:31:36,770 --> 00:31:38,440
Good point.

264
00:31:39,150 --> 00:31:43,320
Why don't you tell me 
what's on your mind, councillor.

265
00:31:43,480 --> 00:31:46,740
There is so much in this world...

266
00:31:46,900 --> 00:31:49,820
...that I do not understand.

267
00:31:51,620 --> 00:31:56,370
See that machine? It has something to do 
with recycling our water supply.

268
00:31:56,540 --> 00:31:59,540
I have absolutely no idea how it works.

269
00:31:59,710 --> 00:32:03,800
But I do understand the reason 
for it to work.

270
00:32:05,300 --> 00:32:09,800
I have absolutely no idea how you 
are able to do some of the things you do.

271
00:32:10,970 --> 00:32:14,140
But I believe there's a reason for that 
as well.

272
00:32:15,020 --> 00:32:20,150
I only hope we understand that reason 
before it's too late.

273
00:32:26,650 --> 00:32:28,320
- Ballard. 
- Is he here?

274
00:32:30,740 --> 00:32:33,330
Neo, it's from the Oracle.

275
00:32:36,290 --> 00:32:37,080
It's time to go.

276
00:32:47,380 --> 00:32:49,550
- Neo! 
- How the hell--?

277
00:32:49,970 --> 00:32:52,140
Bane.

278
00:32:52,300 --> 00:32:53,640
Is something wrong?

279
00:32:53,800 --> 00:32:55,510
No, I'm fine.

280
00:32:55,680 --> 00:32:58,480
I just wanted to catch you to say...

281
00:32:58,640 --> 00:33:00,480
...good luck.

282
00:33:02,150 --> 00:33:03,860
Thanks.

283
00:33:04,020 --> 00:33:06,440
We'll see you.

284
00:33:08,030 --> 00:33:11,110
Neo! Just in time.

285
00:33:11,280 --> 00:33:13,620
- You're gonna see the Oracle? 
- There's no time.

286
00:33:13,780 --> 00:33:15,410
I had to give something to Neo.

287
00:33:16,120 --> 00:33:18,830
A gift from one of the orphans.

288
00:33:19,120 --> 00:33:22,420
He made me swear to get it to you 
before you left.

289
00:33:23,290 --> 00:33:25,750
He said you'd understand.

290
00:33:28,420 --> 00:33:30,550
Thanks.

291
00:33:37,640 --> 00:33:40,560
I was just told you cleared 
the <i>Nebuchadnezzar</i> for takeoff.

292
00:33:40,730 --> 00:33:42,690
That is correct.

293
00:33:42,850 --> 00:33:44,810
Am I still in charge 
of our defense system?

294
00:33:44,980 --> 00:33:46,270
Of course.

295
00:33:46,980 --> 00:33:51,030
I believe I need every ship we have 
if we're going to survive this attack.

296
00:33:51,610 --> 00:33:53,780
I understand that, commander.

297
00:33:53,950 --> 00:33:56,530
Then why did you allow 
the <i>Nebuchadnezzar</i> to leave?

298
00:33:56,700 --> 00:34:01,580
Because I believe our survival depends 
on more than how many ships we have.

299
00:34:04,080 --> 00:34:06,380
Be careful.

300
00:34:35,410 --> 00:34:37,620
Hello.

301
00:34:47,920 --> 00:34:51,460
- You seek the Oracle. 
- Who are you?

302
00:34:54,510 --> 00:34:59,010
I am Seraph. I can take you to her, 
but first I must apologize.

303
00:34:59,260 --> 00:35:00,970
Apologize for what?

304
00:35:01,640 --> 00:35:03,430
For this.

305
00:36:00,740 --> 00:36:02,990
Good.

306
00:36:05,500 --> 00:36:08,670
The Oracle has many enemies. 
I had to be sure.

307
00:36:08,830 --> 00:36:11,040
- Of what? 
- That you are the One.

308
00:36:11,500 --> 00:36:15,260
- You could have just asked. 
- No. You do not truly know someone...

309
00:36:15,420 --> 00:36:17,670
...until you fight them.

310
00:36:18,220 --> 00:36:21,680
Come. She's waiting.

311
00:36:36,740 --> 00:36:38,610
Where the hell did they go?

312
00:36:38,990 --> 00:36:41,700
These are back doors, aren't they?

313
00:36:41,870 --> 00:36:44,780
Programmer access.

314
00:36:45,870 --> 00:36:49,620
- How do they work? 
- A code is hidden in tumblers.

315
00:36:49,790 --> 00:36:54,790
One position opens a lock and another 
position opens one of these doors.

316
00:36:56,550 --> 00:36:59,380
Are you a programmer?

317
00:36:59,550 --> 00:37:01,890
Then what are you?

318
00:37:04,050 --> 00:37:07,560
I protect that which matters most.

319
00:37:27,080 --> 00:37:30,460
Well, come on. I ain't gonna bite you.

320
00:37:30,870 --> 00:37:33,670
Come around here 
and let me have a look at you.

321
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:39,260
My goodness, look at you.

322
00:37:39,590 --> 00:37:42,430
You turned out all right, didn't you?

323
00:37:42,590 --> 00:37:44,800
- How do you feel? 
- I--

324
00:37:44,970 --> 00:37:48,560
I know you're not sleeping. 
We'll get to that.

325
00:37:48,720 --> 00:37:51,430
Why don't you come 
and have a sit this time.

326
00:37:52,140 --> 00:37:56,270
- Maybe I'll stand. 
- Well, suit yourself.

327
00:38:07,410 --> 00:38:09,950
- I felt like sitting. 
- I know.

328
00:38:11,120 --> 00:38:13,040
So...

329
00:38:15,130 --> 00:38:17,540
...let's get the obvious stuff 
out of the way.

330
00:38:17,840 --> 00:38:22,300
- You're not human, are you? 
- It's tough to get more obvious than that.

331
00:38:22,470 --> 00:38:28,310
If I had to guess, I'd say you're 
a program from the machine world.

332
00:38:28,680 --> 00:38:32,890
- So is he. 
- So far, so good.

333
00:38:33,060 --> 00:38:36,230
But if that's true, that could mean 
you're part of this system...

334
00:38:36,400 --> 00:38:38,980
...another kind of control.

335
00:38:39,150 --> 00:38:43,650
- Keep going. 
- I suppose the most obvious question is...

336
00:38:43,820 --> 00:38:47,740
- ...how can I trust you? 
- Bingo.

337
00:38:48,780 --> 00:38:52,040
It is a pickle, no doubt about it. 
Bad news is...

338
00:38:52,200 --> 00:38:55,870
...there's no way you can really know 
if I'm here to help you or not.

339
00:38:56,040 --> 00:38:59,590
So it's really up to you. Just have 
to make up your own damn mind...

340
00:38:59,750 --> 00:39:04,550
...to either accept what 
I'm going to tell you or reject it.

341
00:39:05,840 --> 00:39:08,010
Candy?

342
00:39:10,720 --> 00:39:15,140
- Do you already know if I'll take it? 
- Wouldn't be much of an oracle if I didn't.

343
00:39:15,310 --> 00:39:18,520
But if you already know, 
how can I make a choice?

344
00:39:18,690 --> 00:39:22,730
Because you didn't come here to make 
the choice. You've already made it.

345
00:39:22,900 --> 00:39:27,530
You're here to try to understand 
why you made it.

346
00:39:33,080 --> 00:39:36,040
I thought you'd have figured that out 
by now.

347
00:39:37,790 --> 00:39:40,380
- Why are you here? 
- Same reason.

348
00:39:40,630 --> 00:39:43,380
I love candy.

349
00:39:43,550 --> 00:39:46,380
But why help us?

350
00:39:46,550 --> 00:39:50,050
We're all here to do 
what we're all here to do.

351
00:39:50,600 --> 00:39:53,680
I'm interested in one thing, Neo: 
the future.

352
00:39:53,850 --> 00:39:58,060
And believe me, I know, the only way 
to get there is together.

353
00:39:58,900 --> 00:40:03,820
- Are there other programs like you? 
- Well, not like me, but...

354
00:40:03,980 --> 00:40:06,650
Look. See those birds?

355
00:40:06,900 --> 00:40:10,280
At some point, a program was written 
to govern them.

356
00:40:10,450 --> 00:40:16,290
A program was written to watch over the 
trees and the wind, the sunrise and sunset.

357
00:40:16,540 --> 00:40:19,420
There are programs running 
all over the place.

358
00:40:19,580 --> 00:40:24,050
The ones doing their job, doing what 
they were meant to do, are invisible.

359
00:40:24,210 --> 00:40:28,050
You'd never even know they were here. 
But the other ones...

360
00:40:28,220 --> 00:40:32,300
Well, you hear about them all the time.

361
00:40:32,890 --> 00:40:35,770
- I've never heard of them. 
- Of course you have.

362
00:40:35,930 --> 00:40:40,850
Every time you've heard someone 
say they saw a ghost or an angel...

363
00:40:41,020 --> 00:40:45,610
...every story you've ever heard about 
vampires, werewolves or aliens...

364
00:40:45,780 --> 00:40:48,110
...is the system assimilating 
some program...

365
00:40:48,280 --> 00:40:52,950
...that's doing something 
they're not supposed to be doing.

366
00:40:53,120 --> 00:40:56,120
Programs hacking programs.

367
00:40:56,290 --> 00:40:59,160
- Why? 
- They have their reasons...

368
00:40:59,330 --> 00:41:03,290
...but usually a program chooses exile 
when it faces deletion.

369
00:41:03,710 --> 00:41:07,630
- And why would a program be deleted? 
- Maybe it breaks down.

370
00:41:07,800 --> 00:41:12,340
Maybe a better program is created 
to replace it. Happens all the time.

371
00:41:12,510 --> 00:41:17,470
And when it does, a program 
can either choose to hide here...

372
00:41:17,640 --> 00:41:20,310
...or return to the source.

373
00:41:21,980 --> 00:41:25,270
- The machine mainframe. 
- Yes.

374
00:41:25,440 --> 00:41:27,940
Where you must go.

375
00:41:28,110 --> 00:41:32,320
Where the path of the One ends. 
You've seen it...

376
00:41:33,490 --> 00:41:36,330
...in your dreams, haven't you?

377
00:41:36,490 --> 00:41:39,330
A door made of light?

378
00:41:41,580 --> 00:41:45,130
What happens when you go through 
the door?

379
00:41:47,250 --> 00:41:50,260
I see Trinity...

380
00:41:50,420 --> 00:41:53,590
...and something happens...

381
00:41:53,760 --> 00:41:55,680
...something bad.

382
00:41:55,850 --> 00:41:59,850
She starts to fall, 
and then I wake up.

383
00:42:00,890 --> 00:42:04,770
- Do you see her die? 
- No.

384
00:42:05,560 --> 00:42:08,610
You have the sight now, Neo.

385
00:42:08,780 --> 00:42:11,780
You are looking at the world 
without time.

386
00:42:11,950 --> 00:42:14,360
Then why can't I see 
what happens to her?

387
00:42:14,530 --> 00:42:18,280
We can never see past the choices 
we don't understand.

388
00:42:18,450 --> 00:42:21,620
Are you saying I have to choose 
whether Trinity lives or dies?

389
00:42:21,870 --> 00:42:25,670
No, you've already made the choice.

390
00:42:25,830 --> 00:42:28,380
Now you have to understand it.

391
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:30,380
No.

392
00:42:30,550 --> 00:42:33,800
I can't do that. I won't.

393
00:42:34,510 --> 00:42:36,890
- Well, you have to. 
- Why?

394
00:42:37,470 --> 00:42:40,560
Because you're the One.

395
00:42:42,730 --> 00:42:45,730
What if I can't?

396
00:42:45,900 --> 00:42:47,900
What happens if I fail?

397
00:42:48,480 --> 00:42:51,480
Then Zion will fall.

398
00:42:58,950 --> 00:43:03,830
Our time is up. Listen to me, Neo. 
You can save Zion...

399
00:43:04,120 --> 00:43:07,330
...if you reach the source, but to do that 
you need the Keymaker.

400
00:43:07,500 --> 00:43:08,540
The Keymaker?

401
00:43:08,710 --> 00:43:12,300
He disappeared. We didn't 
know what happened to him until now.

402
00:43:12,460 --> 00:43:16,220
He's being held prisoner 
by a very dangerous program...

403
00:43:16,380 --> 00:43:19,930
...one of the oldest of us. 
He is called the Merovingian.

404
00:43:20,100 --> 00:43:22,970
- And he won't let him go willingly. 
- What does he want?

405
00:43:23,140 --> 00:43:27,980
What do all men with power want? 
More power.

406
00:43:28,690 --> 00:43:31,940
Be there at that exact time...

407
00:43:32,110 --> 00:43:34,780
...and you will have a chance.

408
00:43:35,570 --> 00:43:37,820
We must go.

409
00:43:37,990 --> 00:43:43,370
Seems like every time we meet 
I got nothing but bad news.

410
00:43:43,950 --> 00:43:46,710
I'm sorry about that. I surely am.

411
00:43:47,210 --> 00:43:49,750
But for what it's worth...

412
00:43:50,790 --> 00:43:54,460
...you've made a believer out of me.

413
00:43:55,760 --> 00:43:57,880
Good luck, kiddo.

414
00:44:17,780 --> 00:44:20,780
Mr. Anderson.

415
00:44:21,820 --> 00:44:23,830
Did you get my package?

416
00:44:23,990 --> 00:44:26,160
- Yeah. 
- Well, good.

417
00:44:27,330 --> 00:44:30,210
- Smith? 
- He's not reading like an agent.

418
00:44:30,380 --> 00:44:34,250
- Surprised to see me? 
- No.

419
00:44:34,550 --> 00:44:37,010
- Then you're aware of it. 
- Of what?

420
00:44:38,220 --> 00:44:40,220
Our connection.

421
00:44:40,390 --> 00:44:43,050
I don't fully understand how it happened.

422
00:44:43,220 --> 00:44:46,600
Perhaps some part of you 
imprinted onto me...

423
00:44:46,770 --> 00:44:49,440
...something overwritten or copied.

424
00:44:49,600 --> 00:44:52,310
It is, at this point, irrelevant. 
What matters is...

425
00:44:52,480 --> 00:44:55,570
...that whatever happened, 
happened for a reason.

426
00:44:55,730 --> 00:44:57,400
And what reason is that?

427
00:44:57,860 --> 00:45:01,820
I killed you, Mr. Anderson. 
I watched you die.

428
00:45:01,990 --> 00:45:05,240
With a certain satisfaction, 
I might add.

429
00:45:05,410 --> 00:45:08,910
And then something happened, 
something that I knew was impossible...

430
00:45:09,080 --> 00:45:10,920
...but it happened anyway.

431
00:45:11,620 --> 00:45:14,790
You destroyed me, Mr. Anderson.

432
00:45:16,800 --> 00:45:21,380
Afterward, I knew the rules, I understood 
what I was supposed to do...

433
00:45:21,550 --> 00:45:24,550
...but I didn't.

434
00:45:24,970 --> 00:45:28,890
I couldn't. I was compelled to stay...

435
00:45:29,350 --> 00:45:32,900
...compelled to disobey.

436
00:45:33,480 --> 00:45:37,230
And now, here I stand 
because of you, Mr. Anderson.

437
00:45:37,400 --> 00:45:41,360
Because of you, I'm no longer an agent 
of this system.

438
00:45:41,530 --> 00:45:44,740
Because of you, I've changed. 
I'm unplugged.

439
00:45:44,910 --> 00:45:49,750
A new man, so to speak. 
Like you, apparently free.

440
00:45:50,080 --> 00:45:51,460
Congratulations.

441
00:45:52,210 --> 00:45:54,540
Thank you.

442
00:45:55,130 --> 00:45:59,760
But as you well know, 
appearances can be deceiving...

443
00:45:59,920 --> 00:46:05,090
...which brings me back to the reason 
why we're here.

444
00:46:05,260 --> 00:46:10,140
We're not here because we're free. 
We're here because we are not free.

445
00:46:10,310 --> 00:46:14,230
There's no escaping reason, 
no denying purpose.

446
00:46:14,400 --> 00:46:17,770
Because as we both know, 
without purpose...

447
00:46:17,940 --> 00:46:22,780
- ...we would not exist. 
- It is purpose that created us.

448
00:46:22,950 --> 00:46:25,950
- Purpose that connects us. 
- Purpose that pulls us.

449
00:46:26,120 --> 00:46:27,950
- That guides us. 
- That drives us.

450
00:46:28,120 --> 00:46:32,080
- It is purpose that defines. 
- Purpose that binds us.

451
00:46:32,080 --> 00:46:35,460
We are here because of you, 
Mr. Anderson.

452
00:46:35,630 --> 00:46:40,000
We're here to take from you 
what you tried to take from us:

453
00:46:41,960 --> 00:46:44,050
Purpose.

454
00:46:47,140 --> 00:46:49,010
- What's happening to him? 
- Don't know.

455
00:46:52,060 --> 00:46:55,650
Yes, that's it. It'll be over soon.

456
00:48:42,500 --> 00:48:44,960
- You. 
- Yes, me.

457
00:48:49,130 --> 00:48:52,010
Me, me, me.

458
00:48:56,890 --> 00:48:58,560
Me too.

459
00:51:06,310 --> 00:51:07,350
More.

460
00:52:09,630 --> 00:52:12,460
It is inevitable.

461
00:52:12,880 --> 00:52:14,300
Come on, get out of there.

462
00:52:57,510 --> 00:52:59,840
Are you all right?

463
00:53:00,930 --> 00:53:02,850
- It was Smith. 
- Yes.

464
00:53:03,720 --> 00:53:06,350
- Now there's more than one? 
- A lot more.

465
00:53:06,520 --> 00:53:10,310
- How is that possible? 
- I don't know.

466
00:53:10,480 --> 00:53:12,940
Somehow, he's found a way 
to copy himself.

467
00:53:13,110 --> 00:53:17,320
- Is that what he was doing to you? 
- I don't know what he was doing...

468
00:53:17,480 --> 00:53:20,240
- ...but I know what it felt like. 
- What?

469
00:53:21,160 --> 00:53:24,870
It felt like I was back in that hallway.

470
00:53:25,030 --> 00:53:26,450
It felt like dying.

471
00:53:26,950 --> 00:53:29,830
The machines are tunneling to avoid 
our defense system.

472
00:53:29,080 --> 00:53:33,830
But I believe they will intersect 
certain pipelines to control them.

473
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:36,550
These points of intersection 
are crucial...

474
00:53:36,710 --> 00:53:39,510
...because I believe they're 
vulnerable to counterattack.

475
00:53:39,670 --> 00:53:43,720
Although it has been suggested that 
this is the same kind of attack...

476
00:53:43,890 --> 00:53:47,560
...we've defended for years, 
I urge the Council to realize the truth.

477
00:53:47,720 --> 00:53:51,060
This is the single greatest threat 
we have ever faced...

478
00:53:51,230 --> 00:53:55,060
...and if we do not act accordingly, 
we will not survive.

479
00:53:55,230 --> 00:53:59,240
Commander Lock, the Council is well 
aware of the seriousness of this attack.

480
00:53:59,530 --> 00:54:04,070
You have our leave to prepare our defense 
by any and all means necessary.

481
00:54:04,240 --> 00:54:06,910
- Thank you, Council. 
- However...

482
00:54:07,160 --> 00:54:10,500
...we ask if there's been word 
from the <i>Nebuchadnezzar.</i>

483
00:54:10,750 --> 00:54:13,250
No, councillor. No word. Nothing.

484
00:54:14,880 --> 00:54:18,840
Then we request a ship be dispatched 
to ascertain the fate of the One.

485
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:22,760
I wish that were possible, councillor, 
but I do not believe our defense...

486
00:54:22,930 --> 00:54:26,470
- ...can suffer the loss of another ship. 
- It will, commander, if it must.

487
00:54:26,640 --> 00:54:28,970
It could take one ship days 
to find the <i>Nebuchadnezzar.</i>

488
00:54:29,140 --> 00:54:32,180
- Then send two. 
- This is insane.

489
00:54:32,350 --> 00:54:35,350
Careful, commander.

490
00:54:35,560 --> 00:54:38,900
Forgive my frustration, councillors.

491
00:54:39,070 --> 00:54:42,950
But I wish I were able to comprehend 
the Council's choice in this matter.

492
00:54:43,110 --> 00:54:46,280
Comprehension is not 
a requisite of cooperation.

493
00:54:46,450 --> 00:54:48,910
If you are asking me 
to order two of my captains--

494
00:54:49,080 --> 00:54:50,790
There's no need for such an order.

495
00:54:50,950 --> 00:54:54,500
The captains are present. 
They can answer for themselves.

496
00:54:54,960 --> 00:55:00,210
The Council is calling for two volunteers 
to aid the <i>Nebuchadnezzar.</i>

497
00:55:00,380 --> 00:55:04,550
Are there two among you 
that would answer such a call?

498
00:55:05,840 --> 00:55:09,640
Captain Soren of the <i>Vigilant</i> 
will answer the Council's call.

499
00:55:09,810 --> 00:55:12,730
You understand the situation, 
Captain Soren?

500
00:55:12,890 --> 00:55:15,350
- Yes, ma'am. 
- Thank you, captain.

501
00:55:16,770 --> 00:55:18,190
Is there another?

502
00:55:18,980 --> 00:55:22,690
- Captain, I think we should volunteer. 
- What? You have gone crazy.

503
00:55:22,860 --> 00:55:24,740
- Listen-- 
- Shut your hole, Bane...

504
00:55:24,900 --> 00:55:26,410
...before I put you in one.

505
00:55:27,570 --> 00:55:30,780
Captain Niobe of the <i>Logos</i> 
will answer the councillor's call.

506
00:55:30,780 --> 00:55:32,120
- Thank you, Captain Niobe.

507
00:55:32,330 --> 00:55:37,420
Commander Lock, you have your orders. 
This Council is hereby adjourned.

508
00:55:55,350 --> 00:55:56,770
What can you see, Neo?

509
00:55:56,940 --> 00:55:59,270
It's strange. 
The code is somehow different.

510
00:55:59,440 --> 00:56:01,020
- Encrypted? 
- Maybe.

511
00:56:01,190 --> 00:56:03,150
Is that good for us or bad for us?

512
00:56:03,860 --> 00:56:06,990
Well, it looks like every floor 
is wired with explosives.

513
00:56:07,610 --> 00:56:09,160
Bad for us.

514
00:56:09,570 --> 00:56:11,080
Here we go.

515
00:56:19,080 --> 00:56:22,000
Yes. We are here to speak 
with the Merovingian.

516
00:56:22,460 --> 00:56:26,300
Well, of course. 
He has been expecting you.

517
00:56:26,470 --> 00:56:27,510
Follow me.

518
00:56:48,200 --> 00:56:51,870
A-ha. Here he is at last.

519
00:56:52,070 --> 00:56:55,370
Neo, the One himself.

520
00:56:55,540 --> 00:56:56,950
Right?

521
00:56:57,120 --> 00:56:59,460
And the legendary Morpheus.

522
00:57:00,290 --> 00:57:05,170
And Trinity, of course. 
I have heard so much.

523
00:57:05,340 --> 00:57:08,800
You honor me. Please, sit. Join us. 
This is my wife, Persephone.

524
00:57:09,720 --> 00:57:13,010
Something to eat? Drink?

525
00:57:13,300 --> 00:57:16,350
Of course, such things are contrivances, 
like so much here.

526
00:57:16,520 --> 00:57:19,020
For the sake of appearances.

527
00:57:19,180 --> 00:57:22,650
- No, thank you. 
- Yes, of course. Who has time?

528
00:57:22,810 --> 00:57:27,900
Who has time? But then, if we do not ever 
take time, how can we ever have time?

529
00:57:31,860 --> 00:57:33,620
You know why we are here.

530
00:57:35,370 --> 00:57:40,250
I am a trafficker of information. 
I know everything I can.

531
00:57:40,660 --> 00:57:46,500
The question is, 
do you know why you are here?

532
00:57:46,800 --> 00:57:49,260
We are looking for the Keymaker.

533
00:57:49,920 --> 00:57:54,430
Oh, yes, it is true. 
The Keymaker, of course.

534
00:57:54,600 --> 00:57:57,560
But this is not a reason, 
this is not a why.

535
00:57:57,720 --> 00:58:01,480
The Keymaker himself, his very nature, 
is a means, it is not an end.

536
00:58:01,640 --> 00:58:07,400
And so to look for him is to be 
looking for a means to do...

537
00:58:07,570 --> 00:58:10,740
- ...what? 
- You know the answer to that question.

538
00:58:10,900 --> 00:58:13,030
But do you?

539
00:58:13,240 --> 00:58:15,570
You think you do, but you do not.

540
00:58:15,740 --> 00:58:18,950
You are here 
because you were sent here.

541
00:58:19,120 --> 00:58:22,250
You were told to come here, 
and then you obeyed.

542
00:58:23,420 --> 00:58:25,750
It is, of course, the way of all things.

543
00:58:25,920 --> 00:58:28,590
You see, there is only one constant...

544
00:58:28,750 --> 00:58:32,930
...one universal. It is the only real truth.

545
00:58:33,090 --> 00:58:34,760
Causality.

546
00:58:34,930 --> 00:58:37,220
Action, reaction.

547
00:58:37,390 --> 00:58:41,600
- Cause and effect. 
- Everything begins with choice.

548
00:58:41,770 --> 00:58:43,520
No. Wrong.

549
00:58:43,690 --> 00:58:48,270
Choice is an illusion created 
between those with power...

550
00:58:48,440 --> 00:58:50,530
...and those without.

551
00:58:50,980 --> 00:58:56,450
Our only hope, our only peace, 
is to understand it, to understand the why.

552
00:58:56,620 --> 00:59:00,040
"Why" is what separates us from them...

553
00:59:00,200 --> 00:59:02,500
...you from me.

554
00:59:02,660 --> 00:59:06,420
"Why" is the only real source of power. 
Without it, you are powerless.

555
00:59:06,580 --> 00:59:09,880
And this is how you come to me, 
without why, without power.

556
00:59:10,050 --> 00:59:12,840
Another link in the chain.

557
00:59:13,050 --> 00:59:14,340
But fear not.

558
00:59:14,510 --> 00:59:18,390
Since I have seen how good you are 
at following orders...

559
00:59:18,550 --> 00:59:21,180
...I will tell you what to do next.

560
00:59:21,680 --> 00:59:26,520
Run back and give the fortuneteller 
this message:

561
00:59:26,730 --> 00:59:30,980
Her time is almost up.

562
00:59:32,030 --> 00:59:35,570
Now I have some real business to do, 
so I will say <i>adieu</i> and goodbye.

563
00:59:35,740 --> 00:59:38,240
- This isn't over. 
- Oh, yes, it is.

564
00:59:38,410 --> 00:59:44,790
The Keymaker is mine, and I see no reason 
why I should give him up.

565
00:59:44,960 --> 00:59:49,000
- No reason at all. 
- Where are you going?

566
00:59:49,170 --> 00:59:53,880
Please, <i>ma chérie,</i> I have told you. 
We are all victims of causality.

567
00:59:54,050 --> 00:59:57,380
I drank too much wine, 
I must take a piss.

568
00:59:57,880 --> 01:00:01,010
Cause and effect. <i>Au revoir.</i>

569
01:00:09,270 --> 01:00:10,770
Well, that didn't go so well.

570
01:00:10,940 --> 01:00:13,320
Are you certain the Oracle 
didn't say anything else?

571
01:00:13,480 --> 01:00:15,610
- Yes. 
- Maybe we did something wrong.

572
01:00:16,280 --> 01:00:17,610
Or didn't do something.

573
01:00:17,780 --> 01:00:21,030
No, what happened couldn't have 
happened any other way.

574
01:00:21,200 --> 01:00:23,950
- How do you know? 
- We are still alive.

575
01:00:27,250 --> 01:00:30,500
If you want the Keymaker, follow me.

576
01:01:05,540 --> 01:01:07,290
Not again.

577
01:01:10,710 --> 01:01:13,340
It's all right, boys. They're with me.

578
01:01:14,000 --> 01:01:16,380
These fellas work for my husband.

579
01:01:16,550 --> 01:01:20,380
They do his dirty work. 
They're very good, very loyal.

580
01:01:20,550 --> 01:01:22,090
Aren't you, boys?

581
01:01:22,260 --> 01:01:23,300
Yes, mistress.

582
01:01:23,470 --> 01:01:26,180
They come from a much older version 
of the Matrix.

583
01:01:26,350 --> 01:01:30,520
But like so many back then, they caused 
more problems than they solved.

584
01:01:31,270 --> 01:01:36,270
My husband saved them because 
they're notoriously difficult to terminate.

585
01:01:36,440 --> 01:01:40,490
How many people keep silver bullets 
in their gun?

586
01:01:45,200 --> 01:01:48,410
You can either run and tell my husband 
what I have done...

587
01:01:48,580 --> 01:01:51,160
...or you can stay there and die.

588
01:01:52,080 --> 01:01:54,040
He's in the ladies' room!

589
01:02:00,130 --> 01:02:02,050
Hurry.

590
01:02:27,620 --> 01:02:30,790
- My name is Neo. 
- Yes. I'm the Keymaker.

591
01:02:30,950 --> 01:02:32,870
I've been waiting for you.

592
01:02:38,800 --> 01:02:43,380
Oh! My God! My God, Persephone, 
how could you do this? You betray me.

593
01:02:47,720 --> 01:02:50,560
- Cause and effect, my love. 
- Cause?

594
01:02:50,720 --> 01:02:53,730
There is no cause for this. What cause?

595
01:02:53,890 --> 01:02:58,190
What cause? How about the lipstick 
you're still wearing?

596
01:02:58,360 --> 01:03:01,070
Lipstick? Lipstick.

597
01:03:01,230 --> 01:03:05,070
What craziness are you talking about, 
woman? There is no lipstick!

598
01:03:06,780 --> 01:03:09,450
She wasn't kissing your face, my love.

599
01:03:10,580 --> 01:03:15,040
Aye-yi-yi-yi. 
Woman, this is nothing.

600
01:03:15,210 --> 01:03:20,750
- It is a game. It is only a game. 
- So is this.

601
01:03:20,920 --> 01:03:22,920
Have fun.

602
01:03:29,430 --> 01:03:31,100
All right.

603
01:03:31,260 --> 01:03:33,020
All right.

604
01:03:33,270 --> 01:03:36,060
Let us find out where this goes.

605
01:03:36,230 --> 01:03:39,110
You two, get the Keymaker.

606
01:03:45,610 --> 01:03:47,610
That's a nice trick.

607
01:03:47,780 --> 01:03:49,070
I cannot go back.

608
01:03:49,620 --> 01:03:51,620
I'll handle them.

609
01:03:52,120 --> 01:03:58,250
Handle us? You'll handle us? You know, 
your predecessors had much more respect.

610
01:04:11,640 --> 01:04:13,680
Okay, you have some skill.

611
01:04:15,890 --> 01:04:17,850
Kill him.

612
01:05:18,040 --> 01:05:20,080
You see? He's just a man.

613
01:07:34,880 --> 01:07:37,640
Goddamn it, woman, 
you will be the end of me.

614
01:07:39,760 --> 01:07:43,770
Mark my words, boy, 
and mark them well.

615
01:07:43,930 --> 01:07:49,150
I have survived your predecessors, 
and I will survive you.

616
01:08:09,210 --> 01:08:12,590
- Where are you going? 
- Another way. Always another way.

617
01:08:16,720 --> 01:08:18,590
Close it, quick!

618
01:08:23,390 --> 01:08:25,930
Could we move along?

619
01:08:29,480 --> 01:08:31,060
Run!

620
01:08:46,080 --> 01:08:49,330
Step away from the door.

621
01:08:54,420 --> 01:08:55,710
We owe you for that.

622
01:08:57,970 --> 01:08:59,130
Just like new.

623
01:08:59,430 --> 01:09:00,890
Drop your weapon.

624
01:09:06,270 --> 01:09:08,100
- Stay with him. 
- What about Neo?

625
01:09:08,270 --> 01:09:09,810
He can handle himself.

626
01:09:12,900 --> 01:09:13,980
Get in back.

627
01:09:51,640 --> 01:09:52,810
Shit.

628
01:09:53,310 --> 01:09:54,810
- Operator. 
<i>- Link, where am I?</i>

629
01:09:55,360 --> 01:09:58,570
You won't believe this, 
but you're way up in the mountains.

630
01:09:58,860 --> 01:10:01,150
- Really? 
- <i>It'll take me a while to get an exit.</i>

631
01:10:01,650 --> 01:10:02,700
- Shit! 
- <i>What?</i>

632
01:10:02,910 --> 01:10:05,580
The twins are after Morpheus and Trinity. 
They don't have a way out.

633
01:10:05,740 --> 01:10:09,120
- Where are they? 
- <i>Middle of the city, 500 miles due south.</i>

634
01:10:25,890 --> 01:10:27,470
<i>- Operator.</i> 
- Get us out of here.

635
01:10:27,640 --> 01:10:30,390
- <i>Won't be easy.</i> 
- I know. We're inside the core network.

636
01:10:30,560 --> 01:10:33,190
<i>The only exit I got 
near you is the Winslow overpass.</i>

637
01:10:33,350 --> 01:10:35,440
- Off the freeway. 
- <i>Yes, sir.</i>

638
01:10:35,610 --> 01:10:39,360
- Fine, we'll make it. 
- <i>I should-- Oh, shit! Look out behind you!</i>

639
01:10:44,360 --> 01:10:45,950
- Incoming fire. 
- Down!

640
01:10:54,210 --> 01:10:55,380
Hold on!

641
01:11:12,390 --> 01:11:14,890
Oh, no. This is getting real ugly 
real fast.

642
01:11:15,060 --> 01:11:16,770
Are you watching this, Link?

643
01:11:16,940 --> 01:11:20,570
Yes, sir. There's an all points on you. 
Eight units headed your way.

644
01:11:21,610 --> 01:11:23,570
Any suggestions?

645
01:11:25,450 --> 01:11:27,450
- Turn right. 
- Right, now.

646
01:11:34,910 --> 01:11:37,750
Straight here. 
You'll hit a connecting tunnel to the 101.

647
01:11:37,920 --> 01:11:39,290
- Good man.

648
01:11:39,460 --> 01:11:41,630
You always told me 
to stay off the freeway.

649
01:11:41,800 --> 01:11:44,420
- Yes, that's true. 
- You said it was suicide.

650
01:11:44,630 --> 01:11:46,550
Then let us hope...

651
01:11:46,720 --> 01:11:48,090
...that I was wrong.

652
01:11:59,980 --> 01:12:01,070
- Operator. 
- Link, it's Niobe.

653
01:12:01,230 --> 01:12:02,860
We've been sent to bring you in.

654
01:12:03,030 --> 01:12:06,110
- I need to talk to Morpheus. 
- Believe me, Niobe, he needs you.

655
01:12:06,280 --> 01:12:08,280
- <i>Where is he?</i> 
- Just follow the sirens.

656
01:12:15,830 --> 01:12:17,750
Repeat, they're approaching the--

657
01:12:20,920 --> 01:12:25,130
- We have them now. 
- The exile is the primary target.

658
01:13:28,280 --> 01:13:29,740
<i>Shots fired.</i>

659
01:13:32,370 --> 01:13:34,240
Move!

660
01:15:24,230 --> 01:15:27,440
- We are getting aggravated. 
- Yes, we are.

661
01:16:13,480 --> 01:16:15,490
Trinity.

662
01:16:15,900 --> 01:16:17,030
Get him out of here.

663
01:16:20,660 --> 01:16:22,740
Come on!

664
01:16:39,760 --> 01:16:41,260
Crush him.

665
01:17:11,750 --> 01:17:12,790
Morpheus.

666
01:17:12,960 --> 01:17:14,460
He's okay. Keep moving.

667
01:17:15,460 --> 01:17:17,260
Let's go.

668
01:17:23,010 --> 01:17:25,180
I need a download 
to hot-wire a motorcycle.

669
01:17:25,350 --> 01:17:27,680
No problem. 
One crash course on motorcycle--

670
01:17:27,850 --> 01:17:29,270
Wait.

671
01:17:30,650 --> 01:17:32,100
Cancel that.

672
01:17:32,270 --> 01:17:34,480
You are handy.

673
01:17:34,650 --> 01:17:36,570
Jump on.

674
01:20:03,840 --> 01:20:04,880
She means nothing.

675
01:20:05,050 --> 01:20:08,180
- Find the exile. 
- We have them.

676
01:20:08,510 --> 01:20:10,640
<i>One-Adam-12, please respond.</i>

677
01:20:17,100 --> 01:20:18,810
Get down.

678
01:22:29,820 --> 01:22:31,450
Gotcha.

679
01:22:32,200 --> 01:22:33,280
She's good.

680
01:22:37,660 --> 01:22:39,950
You are no longer necessary.

681
01:22:46,630 --> 01:22:50,340
We do only what we're meant to do.

682
01:22:51,970 --> 01:22:55,550
Then you are meant for one more thing: 
deletion.

683
01:22:56,510 --> 01:22:58,390
Go kick his ass.

684
01:23:48,440 --> 01:23:51,190
Neo, if you're out there, 
I could use some help.

685
01:23:51,940 --> 01:23:53,400
What is that?

686
01:24:23,270 --> 01:24:26,140
Yes! Yes!

687
01:24:32,730 --> 01:24:37,860
We have confirmation from the <i>Icarus.</i> First 
two ships are in position for counterattack.

688
01:24:38,110 --> 01:24:39,160
Good.

689
01:24:40,160 --> 01:24:41,200
Any change?

690
01:24:41,370 --> 01:24:44,120
They hit some iron ore here. 
Slowed them down a little.

691
01:24:44,290 --> 01:24:47,410
- How much? 
- An hour, maybe.

692
01:24:47,580 --> 01:24:50,130
That would give them 
a little over nine hours.

693
01:24:50,960 --> 01:24:52,590
Yes, sir.

694
01:25:25,200 --> 01:25:27,450
<i>There is a building.</i>

695
01:25:27,620 --> 01:25:33,290
Inside this building, there is a level 
where no elevator can go...

696
01:25:33,460 --> 01:25:35,380
...and no stair can reach.

697
01:25:36,050 --> 01:25:42,140
<i>This level is filled with doors. 
These doors lead to many places.</i>

698
01:25:42,300 --> 01:25:44,640
Hidden places.

699
01:25:44,970 --> 01:25:48,600
But one door is special.

700
01:25:48,770 --> 01:25:50,980
One door leads to the source.

701
01:25:59,320 --> 01:26:03,740
This building is protected 
by a very secure system.

702
01:26:03,910 --> 01:26:06,740
- Every alarm triggers the bomb. 
- Bomb? Did he say bomb?

703
01:26:06,870 --> 01:26:09,540
But like all systems, 
it has a weakness.

704
01:26:09,710 --> 01:26:12,710
The system is based on the rules 
of a building.

705
01:26:12,880 --> 01:26:16,250
- One system built on another. 
- Electricity.

706
01:26:16,800 --> 01:26:21,550
- If one fails, so must the other. 
- No electricity, no alarms.

707
01:26:21,720 --> 01:26:24,550
You'd have to take out a city block 
to kill the power.

708
01:26:24,720 --> 01:26:28,430
- Not one, 27. 
- Twenty-seven blocks?

709
01:26:29,270 --> 01:26:31,730
<i>There is a power station.</i>

710
01:26:31,890 --> 01:26:34,150
<i>It must be destroyed.</i>

711
01:26:34,310 --> 01:26:38,650
- There must be some kind of fail-safe. 
- Yes, there is an emergency system.

712
01:26:40,280 --> 01:26:44,070
<i>The core network of the grid 
must be accessed.</i>

713
01:26:44,240 --> 01:26:47,080
<i>The emergency system 
must be deactivated.</i>

714
01:26:47,240 --> 01:26:48,660
<i>What do you need us for?</i>

715
01:26:48,830 --> 01:26:50,080
Neo could take them out 
easier than we could.

716
01:26:51,160 --> 01:26:52,920
- There's no time. 
- Why?

717
01:26:53,080 --> 01:26:56,210
Once the door is unprotected, 
the connection will be severed.

718
01:26:56,380 --> 01:26:58,670
But another connection 
must first be made.

719
01:26:59,500 --> 01:27:03,340
<i>- How long will that take?</i> 
<i>- Exactly 314 seconds.</i>

720
01:27:03,510 --> 01:27:05,090
<i>Just over five minutes.</i>

721
01:27:05,260 --> 01:27:07,510
<i>That is the length 
and breadth of the window.</i>

722
01:27:07,680 --> 01:27:09,970
Only the One can open the door...

723
01:27:10,180 --> 01:27:13,100
...and only during that window 
can the door be opened.

724
01:27:14,350 --> 01:27:15,940
How do you know all this?

725
01:27:16,100 --> 01:27:21,280
I know because I must know. 
It is my purpose.

726
01:27:21,440 --> 01:27:26,950
It's the reason I'm here, 
the same reason we're all here.

727
01:27:37,710 --> 01:27:40,500
Neo, I know something's wrong.

728
01:27:41,170 --> 01:27:43,220
You don't have to tell me.

729
01:27:43,380 --> 01:27:47,140
I just want you to know that I'm here.

730
01:27:50,680 --> 01:27:52,140
All must be done as one.

731
01:27:54,560 --> 01:27:56,230
If one fails...

732
01:27:57,020 --> 01:27:58,730
<i>...all fail.</i>

733
01:27:59,230 --> 01:28:02,900
At midnight, there is a shift change 
in the security of both buildings.

734
01:28:04,280 --> 01:28:07,530
<i>At midnight, we will strike.</i>

735
01:28:08,160 --> 01:28:09,240
Hey!

736
01:28:09,410 --> 01:28:13,370
- You count sheep at home. 
- Why? I get paid to count them here.

737
01:28:23,550 --> 01:28:25,760
Okay, they're inside.

738
01:28:25,920 --> 01:28:28,430
- How much time? 
- Twelve minutes.

739
01:28:31,140 --> 01:28:32,220
Oh, shit.

740
01:28:35,600 --> 01:28:41,060
All of our lives, we have fought this war. 
Tonight, I believe we can end it.

741
01:28:42,570 --> 01:28:44,740
<i>Tonight is not an accident.</i>

742
01:28:46,070 --> 01:28:48,070
<i>There are no accidents.</i>

743
01:28:49,450 --> 01:28:54,490
We have not come here by chance. 
I do not believe in chance.

744
01:28:54,660 --> 01:29:00,250
When I see three objectives, 
three captains, three ships...

745
01:29:00,420 --> 01:29:03,920
...I do not see coincidence. 
I see providence.

746
01:29:04,250 --> 01:29:06,590
<i>I see purpose.</i>

747
01:29:09,300 --> 01:29:15,640
I believe it is our fate to be here. 
It is our destiny.

748
01:29:15,810 --> 01:29:20,810
I believe this night holds 
for each and every one of us...

749
01:29:20,980 --> 01:29:24,320
...the very meaning of our lives.

750
01:29:24,480 --> 01:29:28,650
I want to ask you to do something, 
but I don't know how.

751
01:29:29,240 --> 01:29:31,160
I promise you, if I can, I will.

752
01:29:32,490 --> 01:29:35,830
What if I asked you to stay out of this...

753
01:29:36,790 --> 01:29:38,790
...no matter what...

754
01:29:38,960 --> 01:29:41,290
...to stay out of the Matrix?

755
01:29:42,380 --> 01:29:44,170
Why?

756
01:29:52,390 --> 01:29:53,470
Please.

757
01:29:55,560 --> 01:29:56,890
All right.

758
01:30:00,230 --> 01:30:02,730
What is it, Niobe?

759
01:30:02,900 --> 01:30:07,030
I can't help it, Morpheus. I can't 
help thinking, what if you're wrong?

760
01:30:07,190 --> 01:30:10,490
What if all this, the prophecy, 
everything, is bullshit?

761
01:30:10,650 --> 01:30:14,660
Then tomorrow we may all be dead.

762
01:30:15,080 --> 01:30:17,700
But how would that be different 
from any other day?

763
01:30:27,170 --> 01:30:33,680
This is a war, and we are soldiers.

764
01:30:33,930 --> 01:30:36,850
<i>Death can come for us at any time...</i>

765
01:30:37,390 --> 01:30:39,180
<i>...in anyplace.</i>

766
01:30:39,350 --> 01:30:41,270
Incoming. Incoming!

767
01:30:43,230 --> 01:30:44,860
Incoming!

768
01:30:50,780 --> 01:30:53,240
Now consider the alternative.

769
01:30:53,410 --> 01:30:57,990
What if I am right? 
What if the prophecy is true?

770
01:30:58,160 --> 01:31:02,580
What if tomorrow the war could be over?

771
01:31:03,540 --> 01:31:06,540
Isn't that worth fighting for?

772
01:31:07,670 --> 01:31:10,300
Isn't that worth dying for?

773
01:31:11,210 --> 01:31:13,840
- Time? 
- Three minutes.

774
01:31:14,010 --> 01:31:15,140
Almost there.

775
01:31:35,200 --> 01:31:36,570
It is done.

776
01:31:36,740 --> 01:31:38,030
Find the others.

777
01:31:39,160 --> 01:31:41,410
I got Niobe there. 
They're out of the station.

778
01:31:41,580 --> 01:31:44,250
- What about Soren? 
- There.

779
01:31:44,410 --> 01:31:46,250
They're still inside, but...

780
01:31:47,130 --> 01:31:48,170
They're not moving.

781
01:32:12,320 --> 01:32:14,240
That's it, let's go.

782
01:32:16,360 --> 01:32:18,200
Call Neo now.

783
01:32:22,160 --> 01:32:24,100
- I lost them. They're inside the portal. 
- What about the grid?

784
01:32:29,130 --> 01:32:32,630
Everything is operational. 
The emergency system is rerouting power.

785
01:32:38,300 --> 01:32:40,470
Jesus.

786
01:32:40,640 --> 01:32:44,680
Soon as they open that door, 
it's all over.

787
01:32:44,850 --> 01:32:46,810
The hell it is.

788
01:32:47,560 --> 01:32:48,900
What are you--? Trinity!

789
01:32:50,190 --> 01:32:53,150
I will not wait and do nothing. 
I will not watch them die.

790
01:32:53,320 --> 01:32:55,490
We're talking less than five minutes.

791
01:32:55,650 --> 01:32:58,150
In five minutes, 
I'll tear that building down.

792
01:32:58,320 --> 01:33:01,870
- How much further? 
- Here, just here.

793
01:33:03,160 --> 01:33:07,160
I'm sorry, this is a dead end.

794
01:33:08,330 --> 01:33:10,830
It's gotta be the ugliest hack 
I have ever done.

795
01:33:14,050 --> 01:33:17,170
That's as close as I can get you. 
You better grow wings.

796
01:33:35,780 --> 01:33:36,820
- Operator. 
<i>- I'm in.</i>

797
01:33:36,990 --> 01:33:39,150
Keep moving. Sixty-fifth floor.

798
01:33:39,740 --> 01:33:43,910
You look surprised to see me again, 
Mr. Anderson.

799
01:33:44,080 --> 01:33:49,460
Well, that's the difference between us. 
I have been expecting you.

800
01:33:49,620 --> 01:33:52,540
- What do you want, Smith? 
- You haven't figured that out?

801
01:33:52,710 --> 01:33:58,210
Still using all the muscles 
except the one that matters.

802
01:33:58,380 --> 01:34:01,050
I want exactly what you want.

803
01:34:01,220 --> 01:34:03,300
I want everything.

804
01:34:03,760 --> 01:34:06,260
Would that include a bullet 
from this gun?

805
01:34:06,430 --> 01:34:08,220
Go ahead, shoot.

806
01:34:08,390 --> 01:34:13,690
The best thing about being me, 
there's so many me's.

807
01:34:25,080 --> 01:34:28,700
Christ! What the hell happened in here?

808
01:34:29,580 --> 01:34:31,620
Hold it right there, little lady.

809
01:34:40,970 --> 01:34:42,760
If you can't beat us...

810
01:34:42,930 --> 01:34:44,760
Join us.

811
01:34:46,930 --> 01:34:48,010
Morpheus!

812
01:35:01,610 --> 01:35:04,740
Still no sight of them. 
They only got two minutes left.

813
01:35:18,500 --> 01:35:19,550
One minute.

814
01:35:28,760 --> 01:35:29,810
Come on.

815
01:35:30,970 --> 01:35:32,890
Come on.

816
01:35:33,480 --> 01:35:35,350
Please.

817
01:35:45,280 --> 01:35:46,820
Kill them.

818
01:35:54,710 --> 01:35:55,750
They're in.

819
01:35:55,920 --> 01:35:57,880
<i>I don't believe it.</i>

820
01:36:13,430 --> 01:36:15,560
It was meant to be.

821
01:36:15,730 --> 01:36:21,110
Morpheus, that door will take you home.

822
01:36:29,870 --> 01:36:34,200
You will know which door. 
Hurry, Neo.

823
01:36:39,710 --> 01:36:42,880
Trinity, I got some serious activity 
headed your way.

824
01:37:35,180 --> 01:37:36,560
Hello, Neo.

825
01:37:37,100 --> 01:37:40,900
- Who are you? 
- I am the Architect.

826
01:37:41,060 --> 01:37:44,690
I created the Matrix. 
I've been waiting for you.

827
01:37:44,940 --> 01:37:49,110
You have many questions. Though the 
process has altered your consciousness...

828
01:37:49,280 --> 01:37:51,280
...you remain irrevocably human.

829
01:37:51,450 --> 01:37:55,030
Ergo, some of my answers you will 
understand and some you will not.

830
01:37:55,450 --> 01:37:59,500
Concordantly, while your first question 
may be the most pertinent...

831
01:37:59,660 --> 01:38:03,380
...you may or may not realize 
it is also the most irrelevant.

832
01:38:04,250 --> 01:38:05,880
Why am I here?

833
01:38:06,050 --> 01:38:09,970
Your life is the sum of a remainder 
of an unbalanced equation...

834
01:38:10,130 --> 01:38:12,470
...inherent to the programming 
of the Matrix.

835
01:38:12,640 --> 01:38:16,720
You are the eventuality of an anomaly, 
which despite my sincerest efforts...

836
01:38:16,890 --> 01:38:19,730
...I've been unable to eliminate 
from what is otherwise...

837
01:38:19,890 --> 01:38:24,360
...a harmony of mathematical precision.

838
01:38:24,690 --> 01:38:27,030
While it remains a burden 
assiduously avoided...

839
01:38:27,190 --> 01:38:31,650
...it is not unexpected and thus 
not beyond a measure of control...

840
01:38:31,820 --> 01:38:35,780
...which has led you, inexorably...

841
01:38:36,740 --> 01:38:37,990
...here.

842
01:38:38,160 --> 01:38:42,250
- You haven't answered my question. 
- Quite right.

843
01:38:42,420 --> 01:38:46,210
Interesting. 
That was quicker than the others.

844
01:38:46,380 --> 01:38:49,010
<i>Others? How many? 
What others?</i>

845
01:38:49,170 --> 01:38:51,670
The Matrix is older than you know.

846
01:38:51,840 --> 01:38:55,850
I count from the emergence of one integral 
anomaly to the emergence of the next.

847
01:38:56,010 --> 01:38:58,260
In which case, this is the sixth version.

848
01:38:58,430 --> 01:39:00,890
<i>Five before me? 
He's lying. Bullshit.</i>

849
01:39:01,060 --> 01:39:04,600
<i>There are only two possible explanations. 
There were five before me.</i>

850
01:39:04,770 --> 01:39:06,060
<i>Either no one told me...</i>

851
01:39:07,320 --> 01:39:11,320
- ...or no one knows. 
- Precisely.

852
01:39:11,490 --> 01:39:14,780
As you are undoubtedly gathering, 
the anomaly is systemic...

853
01:39:14,950 --> 01:39:18,370
...creating fluctuations in even 
the most simplistic equations.

854
01:39:18,530 --> 01:39:21,790
<i>You can't control me! 
I'm gonna smash you to bits!</i>

855
01:39:21,950 --> 01:39:23,750
<i>I'm gonna fucking kill you!</i>

856
01:39:23,920 --> 01:39:27,090
<i>You can't make me do anything. 
You old, white prick!</i>

857
01:39:29,380 --> 01:39:30,880
Choice.

858
01:39:31,050 --> 01:39:32,880
The problem is choice.

859
01:39:55,110 --> 01:39:58,740
The first Matrix I designed 
was naturally perfect, a work of art.

860
01:39:58,910 --> 01:40:00,740
Flawless, sublime.

861
01:40:00,910 --> 01:40:04,410
A triumph equaled only 
by its monumental failure.

862
01:40:05,080 --> 01:40:07,500
The inevitability of its doom 
is apparent now...

863
01:40:07,670 --> 01:40:11,000
...as a consequence of the imperfection 
inherent in every human.

864
01:40:11,170 --> 01:40:14,130
Thus, I redesigned it 
based on your history...

865
01:40:14,300 --> 01:40:18,300
...to more accurately reflect 
the varying grotesqueries of your nature.

866
01:40:19,010 --> 01:40:22,770
However, I was again frustrated 
by failure.

867
01:40:24,230 --> 01:40:26,850
I have come to understand 
that the answer eluded me...

868
01:40:27,020 --> 01:40:29,060
...because it required a lesser mind.

869
01:40:29,230 --> 01:40:35,190
Or perhaps, a mind less bound 
by the parameters of perfection.

870
01:40:35,610 --> 01:40:40,030
Thus, the answer was stumbled upon 
by another, an intuitive program...

871
01:40:40,200 --> 01:40:44,100
...initially created to investigate 
certain aspects of the human psyche.

872
01:40:45,160 --> 01:40:51,130
If I am the father of the Matrix, 
she would undoubtedly be its mother.

873
01:40:51,750 --> 01:40:54,050
- The Oracle. 
- Please.

874
01:40:54,760 --> 01:40:58,760
As I was saying, she stumbled upon a 
solution whereby 99 percent of subjects...

875
01:40:58,930 --> 01:41:01,800
...accepted the program, as long as they 
were given a choice...

876
01:41:01,970 --> 01:41:06,100
...even if they were only aware 
of the choice at a near unconscious level.

877
01:41:06,270 --> 01:41:09,690
While this answer functioned, 
it was fundamentally flawed...

878
01:41:09,850 --> 01:41:13,860
...thus creating the otherwise 
contradictory systemic anomaly...

879
01:41:14,030 --> 01:41:16,740
...that, if left unchecked, 
might threaten the system.

880
01:41:17,110 --> 01:41:21,240
Ergo, those that refused the program, 
while a minority, if unchecked...

881
01:41:21,410 --> 01:41:25,500
...would constitute 
an escalating probability of disaster.

882
01:41:25,660 --> 01:41:27,460
This is about Zion.

883
01:41:27,910 --> 01:41:31,580
You are here because Zion 
is about to be destroyed.

884
01:41:31,750 --> 01:41:36,170
Its every living inhabitant terminated, 
its entire existence eradicated.

885
01:41:36,460 --> 01:41:37,510
Bullshit.

886
01:41:37,670 --> 01:41:40,840
Denial is the most predictable 
of all human responses.

887
01:41:41,050 --> 01:41:47,520
But rest assured, this will be 
the sixth time we have destroyed it...

888
01:41:47,680 --> 01:41:51,690
...and we have become 
exceedingly efficient at it.

889
01:42:04,410 --> 01:42:05,700
The function of the One...

890
01:42:05,870 --> 01:42:10,540
...is now to return to the source, allowing 
a dissemination of the code you carry...

891
01:42:10,710 --> 01:42:12,420
...reinserting the prime program.

892
01:42:13,000 --> 01:42:17,000
After which you will be required to select 
from the Matrix 23 individuals...

893
01:42:17,170 --> 01:42:20,420
...sixteen female, seven male, 
to rebuild Zion.

894
01:42:20,590 --> 01:42:25,140
Failure to comply with this process 
will result in a cataclysmic system crash...

895
01:42:25,300 --> 01:42:27,640
...killing everyone connected 
to the Matrix...

896
01:42:27,810 --> 01:42:30,390
...which, coupled with the 
extermination of Zion...

897
01:42:30,560 --> 01:42:34,770
...will result in the extinction 
of the entire human race.

898
01:42:35,110 --> 01:42:39,190
You won't let it happen. You can't. 
You need human beings to survive.

899
01:42:39,990 --> 01:42:43,610
There are levels of survival 
we are prepared to accept.

900
01:42:43,780 --> 01:42:46,580
The relevant issue is 
whether or not you are ready...

901
01:42:46,740 --> 01:42:50,330
...to accept the responsibility for the death 
of every human being in this world.

902
01:42:56,790 --> 01:42:59,340
It is interesting reading your reactions.

903
01:43:00,380 --> 01:43:04,220
Your five predecessors were, by design, 
based on a similar predication...

904
01:43:04,390 --> 01:43:08,850
...a contingent affirmation that was meant 
to create a profound attachment...

905
01:43:09,020 --> 01:43:12,600
...to the rest of your species, 
facilitating the function of the One.

906
01:43:12,770 --> 01:43:15,100
While the others experience this 
in a general way...

907
01:43:15,270 --> 01:43:18,230
...your experience is far more specific...

908
01:43:18,570 --> 01:43:21,440
...vis-à-vis love.

909
01:43:22,450 --> 01:43:24,070
Trinity!

910
01:43:26,370 --> 01:43:30,700
Apropos, she entered the Matrix 
to save your life at the cost of her own.

911
01:43:31,080 --> 01:43:32,120
No.

912
01:43:32,830 --> 01:43:36,960
Which brings us at last to the moment 
of truth, wherein the fundamental flaw...

913
01:43:37,130 --> 01:43:40,210
...is ultimately expressed 
and the anomaly revealed...

914
01:43:40,380 --> 01:43:44,380
...as both beginning and end.

915
01:43:44,550 --> 01:43:46,220
There are two doors.

916
01:43:46,390 --> 01:43:49,600
The door to your right leads to the source 
and the salvation of Zion.

917
01:43:50,180 --> 01:43:56,480
The door to your left leads back to the 
Matrix, to her and the end of your species.

918
01:43:56,650 --> 01:44:01,030
As you adequately put, 
the problem is choice.

919
01:44:01,190 --> 01:44:04,700
But we already know what 
you are going to do, don't we?

920
01:44:04,860 --> 01:44:08,950
Already I can see the chain reaction, 
the chemical precursors that signal...

921
01:44:09,120 --> 01:44:14,370
...the onset of an emotion designed 
specifically to overwhelm logic and reason.

922
01:44:14,540 --> 01:44:19,170
An emotion that is already blinding you 
from the simple and obvious truth:

923
01:44:19,340 --> 01:44:25,840
She is going to die and there is nothing 
you can do to stop it.

924
01:44:30,850 --> 01:44:34,980
Hope. It is the quintessential 
human delusion, simultaneously...

925
01:44:35,140 --> 01:44:38,850
...the source of your greatest strength 
and your greatest weakness.

926
01:44:39,020 --> 01:44:43,360
If I were you, I would hope 
that we don't meet again.

927
01:44:43,530 --> 01:44:44,940
We won't.

928
01:44:52,370 --> 01:44:54,580
We got a serious situation, sir.

929
01:44:55,040 --> 01:44:56,120
Oh, no.

930
01:45:55,770 --> 01:45:59,310
- What was that? 
- It's moving faster than anything I've seen.

931
01:47:03,670 --> 01:47:05,500
Neo, I had to.

932
01:47:05,670 --> 01:47:07,420
I know.

933
01:47:12,470 --> 01:47:15,010
The bullet is still inside.

934
01:47:25,770 --> 01:47:27,690
Trinity...

935
01:47:28,900 --> 01:47:30,610
...don't you quit on me now.

936
01:47:39,790 --> 01:47:42,370
I'm sorry.

937
01:47:48,880 --> 01:47:51,170
Trinity.

938
01:48:01,140 --> 01:48:03,100
Trinity...

939
01:48:03,270 --> 01:48:05,060
...I know you can hear me.

940
01:48:05,850 --> 01:48:08,400
I'm not letting go.

941
01:48:08,560 --> 01:48:10,190
I can't.

942
01:48:11,400 --> 01:48:13,610
I love you too damn much.

943
01:48:42,310 --> 01:48:43,600
I can't take this.

944
01:48:47,350 --> 01:48:50,440
I guess this makes us even.

945
01:49:03,120 --> 01:49:05,080
I don't understand it.

946
01:49:05,250 --> 01:49:08,250
Everything was done 
as it was supposed to be done.

947
01:49:08,420 --> 01:49:11,460
Once the One reaches the source, 
the war should be over.

948
01:49:11,630 --> 01:49:14,460
- In 24 hours, it will be. 
- What?

949
01:49:14,630 --> 01:49:18,970
If we don't do something in 24 hours, 
Zion will be destroyed.

950
01:49:19,390 --> 01:49:21,010
- What? 
- How do you know that?

951
01:49:21,470 --> 01:49:23,510
- I was told it would happen. 
- By whom?

952
01:49:24,520 --> 01:49:27,350
It doesn't matter. I believed him.

953
01:49:27,520 --> 01:49:31,360
- That's impossible. The prophecy tells us-- 
- It was a lie, Morpheus.

954
01:49:33,110 --> 01:49:35,650
The prophecy was a lie.

955
01:49:36,860 --> 01:49:39,860
The One was never meant 
to end anything.

956
01:49:39,110 --> 01:49:43,080
It was all another system of control.

957
01:49:43,240 --> 01:49:46,330
I don't believe that.

958
01:49:46,660 --> 01:49:48,100
But you said it yourself.

959
01:49:49,160 --> 01:49:53,170
How can the prophecy be true 
if the war isn't over?

960
01:49:59,340 --> 01:50:01,800
I'm sorry.

961
01:50:01,970 --> 01:50:05,350
I know it isn't easy to hear, but...

962
01:50:05,510 --> 01:50:08,680
...I swear to you it's the truth.

963
01:50:11,900 --> 01:50:14,610
- What are we gonna do? 
- I don't know.

964
01:50:16,820 --> 01:50:18,030
Oh, no!

965
01:50:27,370 --> 01:50:30,710
- What are they doing? 
- They're just out of EMP range.

966
01:50:31,210 --> 01:50:32,460
It's a bomb.

967
01:50:33,630 --> 01:50:35,840
We have to get out of here. Now.

968
01:51:12,540 --> 01:51:14,420
I have dreamed a dream...

969
01:51:17,460 --> 01:51:20,840
...but now that dream 
has gone from me.

970
01:51:31,890 --> 01:51:34,140
Here they come.

971
01:51:34,400 --> 01:51:36,110
Let's go, Morpheus.

972
01:51:37,520 --> 01:51:40,570
- We won't make it. 
- We have to try.

973
01:51:48,280 --> 01:51:51,290
- Come on! 
- Something's different.

974
01:51:51,450 --> 01:51:53,460
What?

975
01:51:54,120 --> 01:51:55,620
I can feel them.

976
01:52:18,560 --> 01:52:20,150
Neo!

977
01:52:26,320 --> 01:52:29,910
- What happened? 
- I don't know.

978
01:52:35,160 --> 01:52:37,080
It's the <i>Hammer.</i>

979
01:52:48,760 --> 01:52:51,470
He's in some kind of coma...

980
01:52:51,640 --> 01:52:53,890
...but his vitals are stable.

981
01:52:55,100 --> 01:52:57,020
What about you?

982
01:52:57,190 --> 01:52:59,310
I'm fine.

983
01:52:59,480 --> 01:53:01,860
You could use some rest.

984
01:53:02,020 --> 01:53:03,860
No, I'm gonna stay with him.

985
01:53:10,950 --> 01:53:13,580
Lock was right. 
He guessed that the machines...

986
01:53:13,740 --> 01:53:16,620
...would cut <i>off</i> the mainlines 
in and out of Zion.

987
01:53:16,790 --> 01:53:19,540
He thought a counterattack 
might surprise them.

988
01:53:19,790 --> 01:53:23,210
It sounded good. 
I figured we had a shot...

989
01:53:23,550 --> 01:53:26,090
...until someone screwed it up.

990
01:53:26,260 --> 01:53:28,880
An EMP was triggered before 
we got in position.

991
01:53:29,050 --> 01:53:30,930
Five ships were instantly downed.

992
01:53:31,090 --> 01:53:32,890
When the machines broke through...

993
01:53:33,060 --> 01:53:36,270
...it wasn't a battle, it was a slaughter.

994
01:53:36,430 --> 01:53:39,270
Was it an accident? 
Some sort of malfunction?

995
01:53:39,440 --> 01:53:41,900
- No one knows. 
- Someone does.

996
01:53:42,060 --> 01:53:43,820
Who?

997
01:53:43,980 --> 01:53:47,690
Once the machines were done with us, 
they started digging again.

998
01:53:47,860 --> 01:53:50,160
We made a quick pass 
to look for survivors.

999
01:53:50,360 --> 01:53:51,450
You found one?

1000
01:53:53,200 --> 01:53:54,910
Only one.

1001
02:03:48,000 --> 02:03:51,300
<i>Everything that has a beginning...</i>

1002
02:03:51,460 --> 02:03:53,170
<i>...has an end.</i>

1003
02:03:55,590 --> 02:03:58,470
<i>I see the end coming.</i>

1004
02:03:58,640 --> 02:04:02,430
<i>I see the darkness spreading. 
I see death.</i>

1005
02:04:04,560 --> 02:04:07,560
Mr. Anderson, welcome back.

1006
02:04:07,730 --> 02:04:09,730
We missed you.

1007
02:04:09,900 --> 02:04:11,730
It ends tonight.

1008
02:04:18,950 --> 02:04:22,080
<i>You are all that stands in his way.</i>

1009
02:04:23,660 --> 02:04:28,210
<i>If you cannot stop him tonight, 
then I fear that tomorrow may never come.</i>
